# Gate step 1185-9qx6 — data, not code.
#
# Binds the fixture for the release-tier writer/reader contract. Hermetic: every
# arm points the guard at a throwaway index via TILLANDSIAS_CHECK_LOG_INDEX, so
# the verdict never depends on whether THIS host has run the tier.
#
# THE ARM THAT MATTERS IS THE NEGATIVE CONTROL (arm 2): a phase-only pre-build
# run must still read never:release-tier. 1174-6r4k narrowed the reader to
# FULL-tier runs and was right; 1185-9qx6 fixed the WRITER so that narrowing
# never has to be widened. If arm 2 goes green, the guard has been loosened back
# into accepting a pre-build gate as a release-tier answer, and the daily
# exercise will skip the real tier on the strength of it.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking a green ci-full leaves a full-tier record the freshness guard can read (1185-9qx6)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-release-tier-freshness-reads-ci-full.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the release-tier freshness contract regressed (1185-9qx6) — either ci-full has stopped recording the phases it runs outside local-ci.sh (so a green release-tier run reads as never:release-tier, the pre-fix defect measured on macuahuitl 2026-09-14), or the guard has widened and a phase-only pre-build run now reads as a release-tier answer (1174-6r4k); see the failing arm above"
STEP_OK="release-tier freshness writer/reader contract check passed"
# Exit 3 means the guard, the recorder or jq is absent — nothing was examined,
# and the fixture says so by name rather than passing.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=3
STEP_SKIP_DESC="scripts/check-release-tier-freshness.sh, scripts/record-ci-phase-result.sh or jq is absent, so the contract could not be exercised"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:release-tier-ci-full:8"
